ean potential is only  a matter of political will and I know  for sure that again not only Orsola  but also user per L and Jean Michel will  have the determination and the courage  to consolidate our work on the defence  of the European Union the word is asking  us to be a global security provider as I  mentioned cooperative one at the  services of peace but also and here come  to the second point I would like to  highlight also and even more so probably  to be a champion of multilateralism  Europe is a cooperative and multilateral  power by definition at a time when the  idea of a cooperative global order has  come under increasing pressure who have  invested in multilateralism like never  before and we have always invested in  multilateralism this is first and  foremost about the work we have done  with the United Nations and in the UN  Framework we support you and mediations  from Syria to Libya and elsewhere we  work to achieve and implement the Paris  agreement on climate change and the  sustainable development goals we have  saved the UN agency for Palestinian  refugees from collapsing and some work  still needs to be done we are working to  preserve the deal with Iran and that is  as you all know a UN Security Council  resolution and we are exploring  innovative forms of collaboration with  United Nations thank of our trilateral  cooperation with the UN and the African  Union covers many different aspects but  a key vital test for it is the work we  do together with them to empty detention  centers in Libya but multilateralism is  not just about UN system the UN system  is at its core but it is a global  approach to preventing and solving  conflicts in every context in on every  single issue global challenge crisis but  also opportunities we try to invest  always in multi life  cooperative approaches because this is  the only way to find just and  sustainable solutions to the problems of  our times we always put our convening  power to the service of multilateralism  trying to bring the relevant regional  and global for our powers to the  negotiating table or setting up a  contact group we always try to build a  space for dialogue to create the  conditions for a mediated solution with  an inclusive approach and building  processes that are based on full  ownership of all those involved the  people not just the governments or  institutions this is how we achieved the  nuclear deal with Iran back then this is  also how we're trying to save it  today it was the original idea when we  back then set up the International Syria  support group and later with the brasses  conferences on Syria we bring together  different players to try and achieve a  political but also humanitarian  objective this is why we invested so  much in the Middle East quartet and we  continue to do so in difficult  circumstances but again imagine if we  didn't do it it is the idea behind the  International contact group on Venezuela  the quartet with the UN the Arab League  and the African Union for Libya the  regional meetings were organized on  Afghanistan and the list could continue  in all cases we always made clear that  our efforts were aimed at contributing  to the United Nations work being the  United Nations for us the ultimate  framework the center of gravity for all  multilateral work some of our  initiatives have been successful as I  said some other have been less  successful but this has been a truly  systemic contribution we've always  invested in building a framework for  cooperation where it did not exist or  where it was challenged third team that  I would like to mention is the  partnership approach here I have to say  this is something on which your work on  the ground can contribute and honestly  and for those of you that have been  already as of delegation you have  contributed enormously because  partnership is built on trust  even sometimes on personal  and contacts and the sense of being  pleasant every single day of the work  I've always believed that Europe is a  global power but being a global power  does not mean that we alone can solve  all the issues of our times no global  power can do that we all need partners  we need to join forces with those who  share our same interests and values and  I will make just one example on our new  partnership with Africa it is something  I really proud of in these years we have  realized that the old donor-recipient  mentality or even the partnership based  purely on management of migration flows  simply doesn't work it's not what  response to the ambitions the  aspirations the needs of our  interlocutors and so wouldn't work  wouldn't fly we moved from simply  working for Africa to working with  Africa and I can say that today probably  our partnership with Africa starting  with the African Union but also the sub  regional organizations and the  individual countries is one of the  strongest one we have it's even a  friendship it's not just a partnership  and our African friends as we name each  other our brothers and sisters are  coming up with African solutions to  African problems and we're putting our  strengths also our resources behind  their solutions and this is what we have  done for instance with the g5 Sahel and  its joint military force I was just  there just a couple of months ago this  is the logic that underpins also our  external investment plan a largest ever  investment program for Africa and this  is also the spirit of the Abidjan summit  we had a few years ago and the one that  I already mentioned the trilateral  cooperation with the African Union and  the United Nations this approach the  partnership approach makes us more  credible and it makes us different from  most of other great powers it is so  powerful to meet your partner and say I  have no hidden agenda this is what we  share it is what we disagree upon we can  start our work in partnership on a fair  basis where everything is transparent  and you can trust us  sometimes it  difficult what is difficult you see it  and you see it a lot but you don't get  hidden surprises on the way and I think  this is very much appreciated in these  times of unpredictable shifts so  preserving the partnership approach  based on shared interests mutual respect  transparency I believe will be essential  power credibility and also to the  effectiveness of our external action  fourth issue of the land to touch upon  when I took office our focus was mainly  and probably rightly so on responding to  crisis and emergencies in these years we  have shifted the focus on preventing  crisis tackling their long-term effects  and also on investing in the positive  stories around the world we have put  resilience at the core of our action to  make states and societies more capable  of a soar being external and even  internal shocks I could make many  examples but I will only name one right  here on our continent the crisis in  Ukraine is still not over  but in this five years Ukraine has come  a very long way and it is today a much  more resilient country than it was five  years ago our work with Ukraine has a  very strong security component rightly  so but we've also invested immensely in  the country's human development we have  helped create jobs built and rebuilt  infrastructure with libera liberalized  access to the European Union invested in  exchanges between our people between our  universities in this five years we've  put together for Ukraine the largest  Support Package  in the history of the European Union and  it is thanks to that if the country has  not collapsed and has managed to move on  and try to get out of this crisis to  tear your new bases in spite of immense  challenges Ukraine today is a much  stronger country than it used to be I  remember 2014 dramatic year when I  started we were definitely not in the  same place and in general terms  investing on the good stories we see in  the world acknowledging the positive  developments because sometimes we are  perceived rightly so as the ones  pointing out at the difficulties the  work that still needs to be done you  need to do more  reforms on human rights recognizing and  acknowledging the positive steps that  countries governments on already civil  society has made or is making in  different parts of the world I think is  an integral part of our work going and  putting our flag not only on managing or  solving crisis acute hotspots but also  going in places where there might be no  need to be on the headlines but you can  make a lot of impact positive one and  sometimes it's faraway places in the  world but good friends that simply needs  you to be there and say we don't have  problems among us we are friends with  partners it works I think this helps  building a sort of network of  partnerships based on same values and  same interests around the world so I  think another lesson that I've learned  in these years is to dedicate time and  energy not only to the problems but also  to acknowledging the positive stories  the positive friendships we have  developed around the world because if  you it's like in life if you don't  nourish friendship it rays to die  you need to invest a little bit in that  as well when we're appeals decide to  mobilize all our tools the power of our  engagement is immense and sometimes I  have the feeling as Alda was saying that  we underestimated and that we don't  fully realize how powerful we can be  this is true at the other side of the  world  and I'm sure you some of you that I've  served already have good stories to  share on this but clearly even more so  here on our continent just think of the  Balkans we have a clear interest in  bringing the entire Balkans inside the  European Union and we all know that this  is a long process a complicated one  always interesting and lively we'll take  time  we'll take a lot of problem-solving  we'll take a lot of political commitment  on all sides and dedication it took 25  years to solve the name issue between  Greece and north Macedonia but now it's  done thanks to courage leadership  perseverance and also thanks to the  European Union constant support and  encouragement in these years this has  been achieved the same is true  believe for all the Balkans we will need  courage leadership and perseverance and  keeping a very strong daily presence  there every single day every single day  but if we continue to engage we will  finally read the immense opportunities  that unification of our continents could  create reconciliation first and foremost  because as I said several times this is  probably the only place where  enlargement goes back to the original  value of the European Union buildup  which is making peace where war was that  was the original idea of the European  Union and the Balkans that is it how can  countries that were killing each other  literally just twenty years ago can come  together under the same roof the answer  is in the same roof being together is  the only perspective that can make them  live really in reconciliation and peace  but also for as many of us for some of  us so important even more than  reconciliation in some cases economic  development great social development  security this would benefit not just the  Balkans but all of us we need it with  the European Union needed also because  this is countries that are not outside  of our geographical boundaries they are  all neighboring new member states so  it's not even an issue of enlargement  it's an issue of real reunification of  our continent this time I think to be  wise consistent and take the next step  forward the unification of our European  family and let me say on a personal note  I'm really convinced that if we don't do  it I am sure we would regret it in a few  years time one final point in this five  years our external action has changed  the nature of our work has changed  diplomacy is not the same as it used to  be we experienced it every day you have  to be more flexible and creative and  sometimes consider normal things that  we're not even thinkable few years ago  today we know that engaging with  governments is essential has always been  but is not enough  civil society private sector are  essential interlocutors if you want to  have a real  impact on the ground but also local  authorities think of the work we're  doing on climate change how much  relevant the work is with authorities or  institutions that are not state  institutions in these years we've  expanded our action well beyond the  domain of traditional diplomacy and I'm  very proud of the work we've managed to  do with limited resources and I've also  proud of the good cooperation we've  established with the Commission services  on this we've invested in cultural  diplomacy in economic diplomacy in  science diplomacy and the list could  continue these are all fields where it's  only natural for us to use the potential  we have as European Union putting  together all the different strands of  work we already have in place but just  to project them at the external Action  Service level we have engaged with  religious leaders religious communities  just days ago in Finland we met again  with the members of the global tech  panel we have created to engage with the  world of technology and here again the  list could continue that's the universe  of interlocutors out there beyond  institutions that are very much eager to  engage and work with us in many  different fields and I think this is a  potential that we cannot waste  it's our interlocutors change and as the  word changes we also evolve in this five  years we have realized that we must  mobilize our full potential as a union  synchronizing all our tools from  diplomacy to trade policy from  humanitarian aid from militaries and of  course our internal and external  policies no one understand this better  than those of you that have worked in  the delegations before I believe for our  partners in the world there is no  difference between the es the  Commission's DG's Council European  Parliament it's the European Union it's  Europe on that side they hear one  subjects one player that speaks we need  to make sure that the message at  different institutions deliver is  coherent because for our interlocutors I  believe also for our citizens there's no  difference between the different  institutions this is something we have  to to own ourselves first and foremost  you represent the European Union not one  institution or the other and  institutions at the end of the day are  the  service of each other and of the  European citizens and of our purpose in  the world so I believe that it is clear  it has been improved in these years we  are Europe we have the European Union we  must act in a coherent and consistent  manner if we want to be credible and  have a real impact in the world and this  is what makes a true difference in the  way our union works more than our rules  more than our institutional structures  it is our political will that moves the  Union forward and let me also thank here  the commissioners that are worth me with  me in these five years because the group  of Commissioners in the CSS met  regularly every month and as I think had  an impact also in the coherence of the  policies were put in place I've said it  over and over again it's the political  will that moves the Union forward the  European Union is what we make of it it  needs everyone's contribution it needs  every nation every institution every  single citizen needs real people to  breathe life into it otherwise it risks  becoming an empty shell and you are the  European Union face in the world as  difficult as it can be but also as  exciting and potentially rewarding as it  can be as I've had the privilege of  paying for this last five years you can  be the point of reference first of all  for all Europeans in the countries  you're posted in and together we can be  also a point of reference for our  partners all around the world in these  years the world has looked at us  searching for a guide for a friend for  someone to work with sometimes just for  someone to talk to and I believe this is  something that we need to fully  understand the more conflictual the  world becomes the more difficult this  work becomes the more important our role  becomes for all those around the world  that are searching for partnership  cooperative approach for peace and  security but also for social and  economic development in a sustainable  manner so you are and will be the women  and men that make this possible every  single day together with your teams in  every part  of this world that is our common house I  want to thank those of you that have  worked already as head of delegations or  in other institutions in these years and  I want to thank you for all you have  done but also and most importantly I  want to thank all of you for what you  will do in these years ahead for me it  has been an honor and a real pleasure to  work with you in this five years and I  can only wish you all the best for the  interest of the European Union but also  for the interest of the entire world  [Applause]
 

